UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54099647892915
DTSTART:20261020T200000Z
DTEND:20261020T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the CGE and Dr. Dragan Kujundzic (Professor of Jewish\, Germanic and Slavic Studies\, University of Florida) for a double feature screening of The Lemberg Machine (2023) and Inside the Lemberg Machine (2026). The first film\, The Lemberg Machine (2023) was directed by Dana Kavelina and is an innovative stop-motion animated film that invites audiences to engage with and examine the lasting impact of violence\, memory and identity in wartime Lviv\, Ukraine. Dr. Kujundzic's recent documentary\, Inside the Lemberg Machine (2026) was filmed this past May on location in Lviv and dives deeper into Kavelina's film. \n\nAfter the screenings\, Dr. Kujundzic will answer questions and lead a discussion about both films. This event is brought to FSU by the UF Bud Shorstein Center for Jewish Studies\, and the FSU Center for Global Engagement\, Ukraine Task Force and Department of Modern Languages & Linguistics. The screenings will begin at 4:00PM in the Globe Auditorium.
GEO:30.440771;-84.298448
LOCATION:Global and Multicultural Engagement Building (GME)\, Auditorium
SUMMARY:Exploring the Lemberg Machine: A Double Feature Screening
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/exploring-the-lemberg-machine-a-double-feature-screening
CATEGORIES:Arts/Entertainment
CATEGORIES:Film Screening
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261015T235235Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54249285878072
DTSTART:20261020T210000Z
DTEND:20261020T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Thinking about a future in international affairs\, diplomacy\, global development or public policy? Join us for a special visit from American University’s School of International Service\, a top-ranked international affairs program\, and learn about graduate study opportunities\, career pathways and how the FSU Global Citizenship Certificate can strengthen your application. Plus\, enjoy free pizza while you connect with the admissions representative\, Angel Martin\, and explore where a degree in international affairs can take you!\n\nThis event will take place on Tuesday\, October 20\, from 5:00-6:00pm in the Globe Dining Room.
GEO:30.440771;-84.298448
LOCATION:Global and Multicultural Engagement Building (GME)\, Dining Room
SUMMARY:American University's School of International Service Graduate Admissions Campus Visit
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/american-universitys-school-of-international-service-graduate-admissions-campus-visit
END:VEVENT
